+# The Daily Grind — homepage with WebMCP tools
+
+Static homepage for The Daily Grind coffee shop. The page exposes its
+**Seasonal Favorites** menu and an on-page pickup order to browser-based AI
+agents through [WebMCP](https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp)
+(`document.modelContext`).
+
+```
+index.html               homepage: menu cards, order panel, declarative checkout form
+assets/menu.js           menu data + pure pricing/order logic (no DOM, unit-tested)
+assets/webmcp-tools.js   page wiring + WebMCP tool registration
+test/menu.test.mjs       node:test suite
+```
+
+Run locally with `pnpm start` (static server) and tests with `pnpm test`.
+
+## Trying it with an agent
+
+WebMCP is an origin trial in Chrome 149+. For local development enable
+`chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing`, relaunch, and open the site. The
+footer shows whether tools were registered. Google's *Model Context Tool
+Inspector* extension lists and invokes the tools; `window.dailyGrind.tools`
+exposes the same definitions in DevTools.
+
+Without WebMCP the page behaves as a normal menu with a manual order panel.
+
+## Tools
+
+Imperative tools (registered from `assets/webmcp-tools.js`). Results are JSON
+strings shaped `{ ok: true, ... }` or `{ ok: false, error }`.
+
+| Tool | Purpose | Inputs |
+|---|---|---|
+| `list_seasonal_favorites` | Menu with prices, sizes, milk options, caffeine, tags, allergens | `search`, `tag`, `temperature`, `maxPrice`, `maxCaffeineMg` (all optional) |
+| `get_drink_details` | Full details and price matrix for one drink | `drink` |
+| `add_drink_to_order` | Add a drink to the on-page order | `drink`, `size`, `milk`, `quantity`, `notes` |
+| `update_order_line` | Change a line's quantity (0 removes it) | `lineId`, `quantity` |
+| `clear_order` | Empty the order | — |
+| `get_order` | Current lines, totals, and last confirmation | — |
+| `highlight_drink` | Scroll to and highlight a card, optionally with a note | `drink`, `note` |
+| `filter_menu_display` | Show only matching cards on the page | same as list, plus `reset` |
+
+Declarative tool (the checkout `<form>` in `index.html`):
+
+| Tool | Purpose | Inputs |
+|---|---|---|
+| `checkout_order` | Place the current order and return a confirmation number | `name`, `pickupTime` (`asap`, `15`, `30`, `60`), `notes` |
+
+Checkout is a visible, agent-fillable form rather than an imperative tool so
+the consequential step stays reviewable by the person browsing. The form's
+`submit` handler uses `event.agentInvoked` and `event.respondWith()` to return
+the result to the agent. There is no backend: a placed order is recorded on
+the page only and nothing is charged.
+
+`drink` accepts an id (`maple-oat-latte`, `dark-roast-espresso`, `cold-brew`)
+or a name such as `"Cold Brew"`.
